  "term": "thyrotropin-releasing hormone",
  "definition": "Thyrotropin-releasing hormone is a three-amino-acid hormone made by neurons in the hypothalamus. After entering the pituitary portal circulation, it triggers the anterior pituitary gland to release thyrotropin and prolactin.",
